0..78 Comment "//! A thunk crosses by its image: what it captures, and the declarations homed"
79..142 Comment "//! at its world that it names. No former marks a mobile thunk."
143..146 Comment "//!"
147..223 Comment "//! A thunk is code over an environment, and the environment is what crosses"
224..298 Comment "//! with it. Its image is read where it is formed, so a thunk crosses when"
299..362 Comment "//! every capture and every homed declaration it names crosses."
363..366 Comment "//!"
367..445 Comment "//! Each declaration forms a thunk at the seat and returns it to the operator."
446..522 Comment "//! The last two force it or apply it there, so it runs as it runs in place."
523..600 Comment "//! The thunks are closed, or over an integer, a marked report or a handle to"
601..679 Comment "//! an integer. The image\'s three axes are the capture rules, so every capture"
680..740 Comment "//! stands at no region, at ω and at the thunk\'s own world."
741..744 Comment "//!"
745..817 Comment "//! - see: #3265 — `forced` and `applied`, a thunk run at the operator"
818..900 Comment "//! - see: `pathological/worlds/closure-axes.gandr` — what a thunk captures that"
901..912 Comment "//!   stays"
913..994 Comment "//! - cites: [Epstein-2011-towards_haskell_in_the_cloud] — a closure crosses as"
995..1029 Comment "//!   its code and its environment"
1030..1033 Comment "//!"
1034..1186 Comment "//! [Epstein-2011-towards_haskell_in_the_cloud]: https://doi.org/10.1145/2034675.2034690 \"Epstein, Black and Peyton Jones, Towards Haskell in the Cloud\""
1188..1262 Comment "// The operator\'s and the seat\'s worlds, and the seat\'s sealed side of the"
1263..1307 Comment "// exchange, its report alone marked mobile."
